  "text": "[calm] A page that plays itself. Rooms that answer cues. A voice that carries the clock. One component is missing, and it cannot be automated. [short pause] Add one word to the address — record — and the page strips for the camera. Controls vanish. The stage squares to nineteen-twenty by ten-eighty. The preflight runs its checks, goes green… and waits. [short pause] A human hand on a mouse. One click to start the recording. One more, inside the page — a real one; a browser will not unlock sound for a script — to arm the film. Then minutes of a human holding his breath. Fifteen, for the longest film. [pause] One confession. The take does get trimmed: the few seconds at the ends where a hand was still on the mouse. The only cuts in the whole production are the ones that remove the human. [short pause] The preflight in chapter one ran live — this very take, passing its own test on camera. Every film is a page. Every page is a door. [pause] The doors are open.",
